            <ArticleTitle>Torsion of an accessory spleen in an elderly patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>838-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Torsion of an accessory spleen is recognized as a rare cause of acute abdominal pain in childhood. A case is reported which, however, is unusual in that it occurred in a patient of 75, who had had no previous symptoms which might have suggested the presence of an accessory spleen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
